## Accessibility Guidelines

- Use semantic HTML elements (e.g., `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`) to convey meaning and structure.
- Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible.
- Provide descriptive `alt` text for all images; use empty `alt` attributes for decorative images.
- Utilize ARIA attributes appropriately to enhance accessibility without redundancy.
- Implement proper labeling for form elements using `<label>` tags and `htmlFor` attributes.
- Ensure sufficient color contrast between text and background.
- Use `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` to catch common accessibility issues during development.
- Validate accessibility using tools like axe-core or Lighthouse.